      "raw_response": "SUPPORTED\n\nThe abstract presents a study that measured the effect of pharmacist participation on medical rounds in the ICU on the rate of preventable adverse drug events (ADEs) caused by ordering errors. The results show a significant reduction in the rate of preventable ADEs after the intervention, with a 66% decrease from 10.4 to 3.5 per 1000 patient-days. The study also found that nearly all recommendations made by the pharmacist were accepted by physicians. While the study only reports on the ICU setting, the findings suggest that pharmacist attendance at ward rounds may reduce adverse events in wards.\n\nANSWER: SUPPORTED",
